1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:01,028
For a split second,

2
00:00:01,028 --> 00:00:02,167
two black holes gave off

3
00:00:02,167 --> 00:00:03,343
more power than every star

4
00:00:03,343 --> 00:00:04,660
in the visible universe.

5
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:06,300
In 2015,

6
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:07,930
LIGO caught two black holes,

7
00:00:07,950 --> 00:00:10,012
about 36 and 29 times

8
00:00:10,012 --> 00:00:11,000
the Sun's mass,

9
00:00:11,020 --> 00:00:12,119
crashing together.

10
00:00:12,139 --> 00:00:13,299
About three Suns of mass

11
00:00:13,299 --> 00:00:14,655
turned into ripples in space

12
00:00:14,655 --> 00:00:15,823
itself, and those ripples

13
00:00:15,823 --> 00:00:17,462
crossed the universe to reach us.

14
00:00:17,482 --> 00:00:18,086
And that's how,

15
00:00:18,086 --> 00:00:18,794
in one instant,
